id: pm-bwkmp4
title: Allow non-colliding extension leaves beneath core command groups
description: "GitHub source https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1249. A published pm-ops installation reportedly loses all ops leaves when core owns the group. Reproduce group versus leaf ownership through the published package; preserve same-leaf core ownership and remove contradictory self-suggestions. The older alias-collision work intentionally rejected nested grafts; this report requires a finer safe composition contract."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-12T22:29:48.459Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-13T09:49:48.171Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-13T09:49:47.607Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-13T09:49:47.607Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: An extension-only ops leaf dispatches beside core ops; a true same-path collision remains refused with both owners; recovery never suggests the exact refused path.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Allow non-colliding extension leaves beneath core command groups
value: Lower agent recovery cost and preserve safe customizable SDK composition
parent: pm-n7rr
resolution: Unique extension leaves dispatch beside core groups while core leaves remain reserved.
expected_result: Unique extension leaves dispatch beside core groups while core leaves remain reserved.
actual_result: "All 8808 tests passed with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; linked tests, static/graph/record assurance, temporary published-package acceptance, npm/Bun packed SDK consumers, and compatibility checks passed. Hosted review and merge remain pending."
